## Your Task

- **ID**: TASK-260715-2nfz7w
- **Title**: Establish ReluxTunnelCore and thin platform-adapter boundaries
- **Parent**: STORY-260715-l2i2oo
### Description

Create the shared Swift package and minimal provider adapter seams defined by the architecture ADR so packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, memory, and diagnostics work can be implemented once and injected into both Apple providers.
### Scope

In scope: package products and modules; platform-neutral endpoint, configuration, metrics, lifecycle, clock, logging, and cancellation contracts; adapter protocols for packet flow and provider lifecycle; dependency injection; Swift Testing target; compile-only provider composition roots. Out of scope: concrete packet bridge, SSH engine, relay protocol, profile persistence, Keychain implementation, route policy, UI, and speculative abstractions not required by supplied specifications.
### Acceptance Criteria

1. ReluxTunnelCore builds independently of application UI and does not import platform-only frameworks outside explicitly named adapter modules. 2. iOS and macOS providers have thin composition roots that adapt Network Extension lifecycle and packet-flow surfaces to shared contracts. 3. Dependency direction prevents shared core from reaching into containing apps or generated target state. 4. Swift Testing contract tests prove both provider adapters satisfy the same lifecycle and version-message behavior. 5. Package and module documentation maps every contract to a supplied M0 or later specification and avoids implementing future feature semantics.

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md
> Core + adapter boundary design constraints

Establish ReluxTunnelCore as a PURE Swift SPM package + the platform-adapter boundary, per .spec/architecture.md, packet-plane.md, ssh-transport.md, routing-dns-lifecycle.md and ADR-001..012 in .spec/decisions.md. Generator/targets already decided (TASK-260715-3r0993: Tuist 4.202.5; ReluxTunnelCore is SPM; iOS 18/macOS 15).

REQUIRED BOUNDARIES:
- ReluxTunnelCore (SPM library): pure Swift, NO NetworkExtension or platform-only imports. Owns tunnel runtime contracts; the SSHTransport protocol (connect / openDirectTCPIP / openExecChannel / upload — ssh-transport.md; keep the engine INJECTABLE, do NOT pick ReluxNIOSSH vs libssh2 here — that is TASK-260715-1gjxer); the packet-bridge interface (public packetFlow <-> bridge, no utun-FD discovery — ADR-003); the internal-SOCKS component boundary (not a user proxy); and the platform-adapter seam.
- Platform adapter modules (named, thin): the ONLY place NetworkExtension is imported. iOS and macOS composition roots adapt NEPacketTunnelProvider lifecycle + NEPacketTunnelFlow to the shared contracts. The concrete NEPacketTunnelProvider subclasses are LATER tasks (3dv8ea macOS, 2hiabd iOS) and the signed extension targets are gated behind Gate A0/P0. So HERE: define the adapter PROTOCOL + a testable composition root, and prove BOTH adapters satisfy the shared contract via Swift Testing contract tests with the NE surface abstracted/mocked. Do NOT require the generated Xcode workspace.
- Dependency direction: core must NOT reach into containing apps or generated target state; enforce + document (a build/test check is ideal).

DELIVER: the SPM package + boundary protocols, both thin adapter composition roots (SPM-testable), Swift Testing contract tests proving common lifecycle + version-message behavior, and module docs mapping each contract to its spec. Build + test MUST pass via SPM on macOS. Keep numeric/policy values injectable (no final MTU/window/lane/engine). If a boundary cannot be expressed without the gated workspace or an unmade decision, stop-the-line with the exact gap.




