./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-2nfz7w/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md:5:- Platform adapter modules (named, thin): the ONLY place NetworkExtension is imported. iOS and macOS composition roots adapt NEPacketTunnelProvider lifecycle + NEPacketTunnelFlow to the shared contracts. The concrete NEPacketTunnelProvider subclasses are LATER tasks (3dv8ea macOS, 2hiabd iOS) and the signed extension targets are gated behind Gate A0/P0. So HERE: define the adapter PROTOCOL + a testable composition root, and prove BOTH adapters satisfy the shared contract via Swift Testing contract tests with the NE surface abstracted/mocked. Do NOT require the generated Xcode workspace.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-2nfz7w/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md:8:DELIVER: the SPM package + boundary protocols, both thin adapter composition roots (SPM-testable), Swift Testing contract tests proving common lifecycle + version-message behavior, and module docs mapping each contract to its spec. Build + test MUST pass via SPM on macOS. Keep numeric/policy values injectable (no final MTU/window/lane/engine). If a boundary cannot be expressed without the gated workspace or an unmade decision, stop-the-line with the exact gap.
