./.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-1y04r0_shared-tunnel-runtime/TASK-260715-30zng6_record-m1-runtime-contract/README.md:7:In scope: ReluxTunnelCore coordinator boundary, packet bridge and HEV ownership, selected SSH adapter ownership, TCP and DNS consumers, route application handshake, app-message snapshots, concurrency domains, stop idempotency, and M2 or M3 extension seams. Out of scope: implementing the coordinator, repeating M0 engine or packet decisions, UI state design, UDP, lane scheduling, reconnect, and release packaging.
./.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-1y04r0_shared-tunnel-runtime/TASK-260715-lovbdz_implement-versioned-runtime-contract-models/README.md:10:1. Every message has a documented version, maximum encoded size, required fields, defaults, and stable error for unsupported input. 2. Configuration contains only non-secret identifiers and opaque references, with tests proving private-key and passphrase bytes cannot be represented. 3. Capability snapshots independently represent TCP, safe DNS, UDP, route mode, and runtime health without falsely claiming M2 full mode. 4. Round-trip, unknown-field, corrupt-payload, oversize, and old or future version tests are deterministic. 5. The models compile for ReluxTunnelCore, both hosts, and both providers without platform-specific transport types leaking into shared code.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-14lk3y/TASK-260715-14lk3y_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2908:.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_legacy-inventory.md:455:| `ReluxProxy` product, five source files, `Package.swift` | Preserve as a standalone legacy SwiftPM compatibility lane, with the same product/target identity and commands. `TASK-260715-14lk3y` owns coexistence with the generated workspace. Do not fold into `ReluxProxyMac` or `ReluxTunnelCore`. | `TASK-260715-35nc5m` may authorize coexistence, replacement, or retirement; implementation follows only afterward. |
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-14lk3y/TASK-260715-14lk3y_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2936:.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_inputs.md:1:INPUTS: (1) Legacy inventory — .research/260720_legacy-inventory.md and the outcome resource on TASK-260715-1fv4z1 (dependency-free SwiftPM macOS 14 executable, Developer ID hardened-runtime, no sandbox, no NE target). (2) .spec/platform-distribution.md — Relux Works Tuist convention is the default generator unless you record a better-supported choice; planned targets ReluxProxyMac/IOS + tunnels + ReluxTunnelCore + ReluxTunnelHarness + relux-relay. (3) .spec/decisions.md — ADR-017 (confirm Tuist) and ADR-016 (confirm exact deployment targets) are OPEN and must be resolved here with evidence. EXECUTION CONTEXT: macOS-first (iOS deferred) but define both iOS and macOS deployment targets. Evidence-gate invariant: pick exact minimum iOS/macOS from current API/dependency (NetworkExtension, Network.framework, Swift concurrency, HEV/lwIP, chosen SSH engine)/device/Xcode/CI evidence, not preference. If any required claim is unverifiable, set the task blocked with the exact evidence gap — do not guess.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-14lk3y/TASK-260715-14lk3y_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2938:EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1r0fxv_build-disposable-macos-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:7:In scope: approved Gate P0 identifiers and profiles; embedded packet-tunnel extension; NETunnelProviderManager save, load, enable, start, status, app-message, and stop paths; one versioned provider response; privacy-safe logs; deterministic build and archive inspection. Out of scope: modifying the current ReluxProxy executable, packet forwarding, HEV, SSH, relay, Developer ID distribution, notarization, full sandbox design, or production UX.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-14lk3y/TASK-260715-14lk3y_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2939:EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:10:1. An architecture decision records the chosen generator, exact supported deployment targets, target graph, module ownership, dependency direction, configuration strategy, and reasons against viable alternatives. 2. Clean generation produces buildable ReluxProxyMac, ReluxProxyMacTunnel, ReluxProxyIOS, ReluxProxyIOSTunnel, ReluxTunnelCore, ReluxTunnelHarness, relux-relay, and protocol-test targets with deterministic identifiers and schemes. 3. Both providers are thin adapters that depend on shared core contracts and do not duplicate packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, or memory state machines. 4. Native Swift and C dependencies can be pinned, licensed, and linked without dynamic-library or App Store extension violations. 5. Credential-free CI or local verification builds every target and runs shared tests; signed physical-device configurations consume Gate P0 identities without committing secrets. 6. The existing SwiftPM tests, manual SOCKS app build, defaults, and release path remain reproducible until an explicit migration decision says otherwise. 7. Developer documentation explains generation, target ownership, signing inputs, artifact locations, and how to run the harness.
