./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2598:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1r0fxv_build-disposable-macos-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:4:Create a minimal, explicitly disposable macOS containing app and NEPacketTunnelProvider target that exercise only configuration, provider launch, versioned app-message response, and clean stop on Apple silicon. Keep it separate from the current shipped menu-bar SOCKS app and the later generated production workspace.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2599:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1r0fxv_build-disposable-macos-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:7:In scope: approved Gate P0 identifiers and profiles; embedded packet-tunnel extension; NETunnelProviderManager save, load, enable, start, status, app-message, and stop paths; one versioned provider response; privacy-safe logs; deterministic build and archive inspection. Out of scope: modifying the current ReluxProxy executable, packet forwarding, HEV, SSH, relay, Developer ID distribution, notarization, full sandbox design, or production UX.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2604:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1jckn0_build-disposable-ios-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:7:In scope: approved Gate P0 identifiers and profiles; NETunnelProviderManager save, load, enable, start, status, app-message, and stop paths; one provider protocol and version response; privacy-safe logging; deterministic build and archive instructions; public Apple APIs. Out of scope: packet reads or writes, routes or DNS beyond the minimum harmless launch configuration, HEV, SSH, relay, profile editing UX, reusable production architecture, TestFlight, and private APIs.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2685:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:7:In scope: current-state and migration inventory; Tuist-versus-alternative and deployment-target evidence; target and configuration graph; iOS and macOS host and packet-tunnel targets; ReluxTunnelCore Swift package; ReluxTunnelHarness CLI; portable relux-relay and protocol-test target shells; signing configuration seams; pinned native dependency integration strategy; clean generation, build, and test verification; legacy SwiftPM and release-path preservation; developer documentation. Out of scope: production packet forwarding, SSH engine selection, UDP relay protocol implementation, profile UX migration, full release automation, App Store submission, and retirement of the existing system-SSH app.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2686:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:10:1. An architecture decision records the chosen generator, exact supported deployment targets, target graph, module ownership, dependency direction, configuration strategy, and reasons against viable alternatives. 2. Clean generation produces buildable ReluxProxyMac, ReluxProxyMacTunnel, ReluxProxyIOS, ReluxProxyIOSTunnel, ReluxTunnelCore, ReluxTunnelHarness, relux-relay, and protocol-test targets with deterministic identifiers and schemes. 3. Both providers are thin adapters that depend on shared core contracts and do not duplicate packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, or memory state machines. 4. Native Swift and C dependencies can be pinned, licensed, and linked without dynamic-library or App Store extension violations. 5. Credential-free CI or local verification builds every target and runs shared tests; signed physical-device configurations consume Gate P0 identities without committing secrets. 6. The existing SwiftPM tests, manual SOCKS app build, defaults, and release path remain reproducible until an explicit migration decision says otherwise. 7. Developer documentation explains generation, target ownership, signing inputs, artifact locations, and how to run the harness.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2697:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-uyju7n_add-macos-host-and-packet-tunnel-targets/README.md:7:In scope: macOS containing-app target; embedded NEPacketTunnelProvider target; bundle identifiers; App Group and Keychain entitlement configuration; minimum platform; host-provider version compatibility constant; empty provider start, app-message, and stop stubs needed for build verification; target-specific resources and tests. Out of scope: migrating the legacy UI, packet reads, routes, DNS, HEV, SSH, relay, production state machines, Developer ID signing, and notarization.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2710:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-33oofa_add-ios-host-and-packet-tunnel-targets/README.md:7:In scope: iOS containing-app target; embedded NEPacketTunnelProvider target; bundle identifiers; App Group and Keychain entitlement configuration; minimum platform; host-provider version compatibility constant; empty provider start, app-message, and stop stubs needed for build verification; target-specific resources and tests. Out of scope: product UI, packet reads, routes, DNS, HEV, SSH, relay, production lifecycle state machines, TestFlight, and App Store submission.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3r0993/TASK-260715-3r0993_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:2719:.task-board/EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-anxje6_continuous-integration-quality-gates/TASK-260717-1s2eiz_bootstrap-repo-ci-board-spec-and-core-validation/README.md:4:Stand up minimal GitHub Actions CI on the relux-tunnel repo from day one, before the full quality-gate pipeline exists. Runs on push/PR: task-board validate (board structural integrity), .spec presence/link check, YAML lint of workflows, and — once ReluxTunnelCore SwiftPM target exists — swift build/test of the shared core. Hardened defaults: least-privilege GITHUB_TOKEN permissions, pinned action major versions, concurrency guard. AC: workflow present and green on a clean checkout; validates board + specs with no Apple credentials required; documented as the seed that the full CI story (harden-github-actions, target build matrix, release orchestration) extends, not replaces. Autonomous end-to-end.
