./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3602:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1r0fxv_build-disposable-macos-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:7:In scope: approved Gate P0 identifiers and profiles; embedded packet-tunnel extension; NETunnelProviderManager save, load, enable, start, status, app-message, and stop paths; one versioned provider response; privacy-safe logs; deterministic build and archive inspection. Out of scope: modifying the current ReluxProxy executable, packet forwarding, HEV, SSH, relay, Developer ID distribution, notarization, full sandbox design, or production UX.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3611:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-1jckn0_build-disposable-ios-packet-tunnel-probe/README.md:4:Create a minimal, explicitly disposable iOS containing app and NEPacketTunnelProvider target that exercise only configuration, provider launch, versioned app-message response, and clean stop. The probe exists to test signing and entitlement viability before the production generated workspace.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3619:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-pmww4f_add-relux-tunnel-harness-target/README.md:4:Create the fast macOS command-line harness target that hosts ReluxTunnelCore components for packet, SSH, relay, fault-injection, and metric experiments without requiring a Network Extension lifecycle for every iteration.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3621:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-pmww4f_add-relux-tunnel-harness-target/README.md:10:1. ReluxTunnelHarness builds from the generated workspace and links the same ReluxTunnelCore products intended for providers. 2. A no-op smoke command records source revision, dependency revisions, configuration, duration, platform, and metric schema in deterministic machine-readable output. 3. Signal cancellation and normal exit release temporary files, sockets, and tasks with tested exit codes. 4. Subcommands can inject clocks, transports, packet endpoints, pressure signals, and fault policies without importing app UI. 5. Swift Testing covers argument validation, result-schema versioning, cancellation, and cleanup.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3650:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_establish-relux-tunnel-core-and-platform-adapter-boundaries/README.md:7:In scope: package products and modules; platform-neutral endpoint, configuration, metrics, lifecycle, clock, logging, and cancellation contracts; adapter protocols for packet flow and provider lifecycle; dependency injection; Swift Testing target; compile-only provider composition roots. Out of scope: concrete packet bridge, SSH engine, relay protocol, profile persistence, Keychain implementation, route policy, UI, and speculative abstractions not required by supplied specifications.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3651:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_establish-relux-tunnel-core-and-platform-adapter-boundaries/README.md:10:1. ReluxTunnelCore builds independently of application UI and does not import platform-only frameworks outside explicitly named adapter modules. 2. iOS and macOS providers have thin composition roots that adapt Network Extension lifecycle and packet-flow surfaces to shared contracts. 3. Dependency direction prevents shared core from reaching into containing apps or generated target state. 4. Swift Testing contract tests prove both provider adapters satisfy the same lifecycle and version-message behavior. 5. Package and module documentation maps every contract to a supplied M0 or later specification and avoids implementing future feature semantics.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3688:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-32umrc_record-generated-project-architecture-adr/README.md:7:In scope: target graph; product and bundle ownership; host-to-extension embedding; ReluxTunnelCore boundaries; platform adapters; native dependency direction; harness and relay targets; configuration and scheme matrix; signing-input seams; versioning; generated versus checked-in files; test ownership; migration sequencing. Out of scope: implementing the workspace, detailed packet or SSH algorithms, release-pipeline design, and changing Gate A0 or P0 conclusions.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3693:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-sbrrp7_add-credential-free-project-build-validation/README.md:7:In scope: pinned-tool bootstrap; generation drift check; macOS host and provider build; iOS simulator host and provider build; device archive or build with signing disabled where supported; ReluxTunnelCore and harness tests; relay matrix smoke; static entitlement and embedding inspection; legacy SwiftPM regression; artifact and log locations. Out of scope: production certificates, physical-device Gate P0 repetition, TestFlight, notarization, DMG release publication, full SBOM policy, and packet or SSH feature tests.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3819:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:4:Replace the single-target SwiftPM-only project shape with a reproducibly generated Apple workspace foundation that can embed iOS and macOS packet-tunnel extensions while preserving the currently shipped macOS SOCKS application until a separate migration decision retires or replaces it. Establish thin platform adapters, a shared ReluxTunnelCore boundary, native dependency seams, a fast macOS harness, and relay target placeholders without implementing production tunnel behavior.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3820:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:7:In scope: current-state and migration inventory; Tuist-versus-alternative and deployment-target evidence; target and configuration graph; iOS and macOS host and packet-tunnel targets; ReluxTunnelCore Swift package; ReluxTunnelHarness CLI; portable relux-relay and protocol-test target shells; signing configuration seams; pinned native dependency integration strategy; clean generation, build, and test verification; legacy SwiftPM and release-path preservation; developer documentation. Out of scope: production packet forwarding, SSH engine selection, UDP relay protocol implementation, profile UX migration, full release automation, App Store submission, and retirement of the existing system-SSH app.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3821:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/README.md:10:1. An architecture decision records the chosen generator, exact supported deployment targets, target graph, module ownership, dependency direction, configuration strategy, and reasons against viable alternatives. 2. Clean generation produces buildable ReluxProxyMac, ReluxProxyMacTunnel, ReluxProxyIOS, ReluxProxyIOSTunnel, ReluxTunnelCore, ReluxTunnelHarness, relux-relay, and protocol-test targets with deterministic identifiers and schemes. 3. Both providers are thin adapters that depend on shared core contracts and do not duplicate packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, or memory state machines. 4. Native Swift and C dependencies can be pinned, licensed, and linked without dynamic-library or App Store extension violations. 5. Credential-free CI or local verification builds every target and runs shared tests; signed physical-device configurations consume Gate P0 identities without committing secrets. 6. The existing SwiftPM tests, manual SOCKS app build, defaults, and release path remain reproducible until an explicit migration decision says otherwise. 7. Developer documentation explains generation, target ownership, signing inputs, artifact locations, and how to run the harness.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3844:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-uyju7n_add-macos-host-and-packet-tunnel-targets/README.md:7:In scope: macOS containing-app target; embedded NEPacketTunnelProvider target; bundle identifiers; App Group and Keychain entitlement configuration; minimum platform; host-provider version compatibility constant; empty provider start, app-message, and stop stubs needed for build verification; target-specific resources and tests. Out of scope: migrating the legacy UI, packet reads, routes, DNS, HEV, SSH, relay, production state machines, Developer ID signing, and notarization.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3878:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-33oofa_add-ios-host-and-packet-tunnel-targets/README.md:7:In scope: iOS containing-app target; embedded NEPacketTunnelProvider target; bundle identifiers; App Group and Keychain entitlement configuration; minimum platform; host-provider version compatibility constant; empty provider start, app-message, and stop stubs needed for build verification; target-specific resources and tests. Out of scope: product UI, packet reads, routes, DNS, HEV, SSH, relay, production lifecycle state machines, TestFlight, and App Store submission.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3930:.task-board/EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-anxje6_continuous-integration-quality-gates/TASK-260717-1s2eiz_bootstrap-repo-ci-board-spec-and-core-validation/README.md:4:Stand up minimal GitHub Actions CI on the relux-tunnel repo from day one, before the full quality-gate pipeline exists. Runs on push/PR: task-board validate (board structural integrity), .spec presence/link check, YAML lint of workflows, and — once ReluxTunnelCore SwiftPM target exists — swift build/test of the shared core. Hardened defaults: least-privilege GITHUB_TOKEN permissions, pinned action major versions, concurrency guard. AC: workflow present and green on a clean checkout; validates board + specs with no Apple credentials required; documented as the seed that the full CI story (harden-github-actions, target build matrix, release orchestration) extends, not replaces. Autonomous end-to-end.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1fv4z1/TASK-260715-1fv4z1_spawn-log_-analyst--researcher--codex-.log:3992:.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/TASK-260715-1q4qhw_record-vpn-configuration-lifecycle-contract/README.md:4:Produce the task-scoped contract for how both containing apps own one NETunnelProviderManager configuration and how both NEPacketTunnelProvider adapters delegate to the shared runtime. Define identity, persistence, permission, command, status, app-message, error, stop, and cleanup behavior before platform implementation.
